Source: omx-contract
Section: libdevel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               nodejs,
               node-typescript (>= 4.8.4~), node-typescript (<< 7~)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/Open-Mixer/omx-contract
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: omx-contract-data
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Section: misc
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Breaks: libomx-contract-dev (<< ${source:Version}), omx-plugins-contract (<< 0.19.3~)
Replaces: libomx-contract-dev (<< ${source:Version})
Description: OpenMixer declarations read at run time: contract directory, schema
 A fader range, a default, a plugin parameter, a supported sample rate: in
 OpenMixer each of these is written down once, in omx-contract, and everything
 else reads it. The declarations are plain JSON with a JSON Schema.
 .
 This package holds the files a program reads at run time: omx-contract's
 own package of the contract directory
 (/usr/share/omx-contract/contract.d/3/omx-contract/, where every owner
 installs its definitions beside it), the JSON Schema, the resolved json
 render, the vocabulary's schema fragment and the resource hints' Turtle,
 under /usr/share/omx-contract. A package that reads them at run time
 depends on this one, never on the development package.
 .
 Its documentation is on openmixer.org.

Package: libomx-contract-dev
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, omx-contract-data (= ${source:Version})
Recommends: omx-contract (= ${source:Version})
Breaks: libomxdsp-dev (<< 0.25.0~), libomx-clap-core-dev (<< 0.13.0~), omx-plugins-dev (<< 0.13.0~)
Description: one shared source of truth for every OpenMixer knob, range, default
 A fader range, a default, a plugin parameter, a supported sample rate: in
 OpenMixer each of these is written down once, in omx-contract, and everything
 else reads it. That is why the console, the DSP library and the plugins agree
 on what a knob does and how far it turns. The declarations are plain JSON with
 a JSON Schema, so tools in any language can read them, and they are rendered
 as C headers for the code that is built from them.
 .
 This package holds the c render under /usr/include/omxcontract,
 omx-contract.pc and install-contract-dir.sh, which an owner's build
 installs its definitions with. The data it builds against is
 omx-contract-data, which it depends on. A consumer requires it at a floor,
 the lowest release whose declarations it builds against.
 .
 Its documentation is on openmixer.org.

Package: omx-contract
Architecture: all
Section: devel
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, nodejs, omx-contract-data (= ${source:Version})
Recommends: pkgconf | pkg-config
Description: command that checks and renders the OpenMixer declarations
 A fader range, a default, a plugin parameter, a supported sample rate: in
 OpenMixer each of these is written down once, in omx-contract, and everything
 else reads it. The declarations are plain JSON with a JSON Schema.
 .
 This package holds the omx-contract command, which validates, formats and
 renders the declarations, and reads the contract directory the packages
 install their definitions into as one checked set. It carries the npm
 packages it runs on (ajv and its dependencies), so it needs node and
 nothing else.
 .
 Its documentation is on openmixer.org.

Package: omx-contract-l10n-ca
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Section: localization
Depends: omx-contract-data (= ${source:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Breaks: omx-contract-data (<< 3.16.0~)
Replaces: omx-contract-data (<< 3.16.0~)
Description: Catalan sentences of the OpenMixer declarations' codes and words
 The Catalan catalog of omx-contract's codes and words
 (/usr/share/omx-contract/catalogs/ca.json): a surface shows these sentences
 on a host in that language, and the English source sentence for any key the
 catalog lacks.

